---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { zooEntries } from "../../data/zoo";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Numerical Zoo | CMNA"
  description="A curated collection of functions, matrices, and differential equations that expose interesting numerical behavior."
>
  <header class="page-head zoo-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Numerical Zoo</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Well-behaved mathematics. Occasionally feral computation.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        These are not here because they are representative homework problems. They
        are here because each one makes some numerical assumption visible, usually by
        refusing to cooperate with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell two-column">
      <article class="content">
        <p>
          Numerical analysis has a useful cast of recurring examples. Some are
          famous because a perfectly innocent formula becomes ill conditioned. Some
          expose cancellation, instability, locality, or the consequences of a bad
          starting value. A few are simply very good at making an algorithm admit
          what it was assuming all along.
        </p>
        <p>
          The entries here are worked problems rather than dictionary definitions.
          Each one starts with the object, works far enough by hand to identify the
          mechanism, gives R code, and points into the CMNA laboratories where the
          problem can be pushed around.
        </p>
      </article>
      <aside class="callout">
        <strong>Please feed the animals.</strong>
        <p>
          Change parameters, representations, starting values, node locations, and
          step sizes. A canonical example is only useful if we make it misbehave for
          ourselves.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell zoo-grid">
      {zooEntries.map((entry) => (
        <article class="zoo-card">
          <span>{entry.kind}</span>
          <h2>{entry.title}</h2>
          <p>{entry.subtitle}</p>
          <a href={"/zoo/" + entry.slug + "/"}>Open cage →</a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
